  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "⚙️ Steampunk Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for steampunk characters, airships, inventions and the companies that build them."
    },
    "intro": "Steampunk takes the Victorian age and gives it more steam, more brass and far more airships. This **steampunk name generator** names characters with a proper title, airships, improbable inventions and the ironworks and learned societies behind them.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Where steampunk comes from",
        "content": "<p>Steampunk is the Victorian age with more steam, more brass and far more airships, and the word was a joke.</p><ul><li><strong>The name:</strong> the writer K. W. Jeter coined it in a 1987 letter to the science fiction magazine <em>Locus</em>, as a play on cyberpunk, for Victorian fantasies he and his friends were writing.</li><li><strong>The roots</strong> are older: Jules Verne's submarines and H. G. Wells's time machine were science fiction written in the age of steam.</li><li><strong>The look</strong> of goggles, gears and top hats grew up in fashion and art from the 2000s.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Naming steampunk things",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Characters</strong> get grand Victorian first names, a profession and an industrial surname: Professor Thaddeus Brassworth, Inspector Archibald Hackett.</li><li><strong>Airships</strong> get ship prefixes. HMA, \"His Majesty's Airship\", was a real prefix for early British airships; SS is the steamship's.</li><li><strong>Inventions</strong> are patented, as real Victorian ones were: Pennyfeather's Patent Aetheric Kettle.</li><li><strong>Companies and societies</strong> are proud and long-winded, as Victorian firms liked to be.</li></ul><p>Famous names like Phileas Fogg and Captain Nemo, and real inventors like Tesla and Lovelace, are left out. For real Victorian names, try the <a href=\"victorian-name-generator.html\">Victorian Name Generator</a>, and for other ships, the <a href=\"spaceship-name-generator.html\">Spaceship Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For the rest of the future, see all the <a href=\"../categories/scifi-names.html\">sci-fi name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Who invented the word steampunk?",
        "answer": "The writer K. W. Jeter, in a 1987 letter to Locus magazine, as a play on cyberpunk."
      },
      {
        "question": "What's a good steampunk airship name?",
        "answer": "A ship prefix and something that flies or sings: HMA Copper Dragonfly, the Whistling Albatross."
      },
      {
        "question": "What's a good steampunk character name?",
        "answer": "A grand Victorian first name with a title and an industrial surname, like Professor Thaddeus Brassworth."
      }
    ]
